    "result_text": "All tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS, 5 tests, 0 failures), including the two new `AcceptanceTest` owner-segment cases.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field on the owner response, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`, keeping each piece of logic in a small, single-responsibility unit and reusing existing derivations.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerSegmentResolver`** (new, `util/`) \u2014 a small pure resolver that composes the segment from a membership level and locality: `PREMIUM` at level \u2265 3 else `STANDARD`, `METRO` for a known region else `REGIONAL`. Mirrors the style of the sibling resolvers (`TimezoneResolver`, `LocalityResolver`).\n\n2. **`LocalityResolver.isKnownRegion(...)`** \u2014 added a public helper next to `rangeForRegion(...)` so \"is this one of NSW/VIC/QLD\" is answered by the class that owns the region table, rather than string-comparing against `UNKNOWN` elsewhere.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added an `ownerSegment` mapping plus a `formatOwnerSegment(owner)` default that reuses the already-present `computeMembershipLevel(owner)` (effective, cap-applied level, matching the exposed `membershipLevel`) and `formatLocality(owner)` \u2014 no duplicated derivation.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `ownerSegment` property so the generated `OwnerDto` carries and serializes it.\n\nThe resolver keys off the DTO's effective `membershipLevel` and `locality`, so the segment stays consistent with the other exposed fields.",
